      "writtenOn": "2021-02-10T09:03:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure but not necessarily in the shape of a non-null array. ConnectivityService#startLegacyVpn calls Vpn#startLegacyVpn with a null argument, even after this patch. In a sense it still has an underlying network, but ISTM this comment is meant in the spirit that it must have a non-null array in the context of this test.\n\nSo :\n- If the comment here means legacy VPN will no longer work when passed null as underlying (which I see no reason for, but anyway) then you may have to fix CS#startLegacyVpn.\n- If not, then I don\u0027t see what\u0027s wrong with just calling setUnderlyingNetworks(null) here (and possibly in LockdownVpnTracker:229)\n\n(if this has to do with the new sendLegacyLockdownBroadcast reading from vpnNai.declaredUnderlyingNetworks, this is set to contain the default network immediately when null is received)",
